WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.610
You don’t need to take a trip to the Upside
Down to spot these spooky details in the new

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.280
“Stranger Things” trailer.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.280
Freddy Krueger?

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:10.429
Hair metal in another world?

00:00:10.429 --> 00:00:15.879
Here are the small details you missed in the
"Stranger Things" 4 volume 1 trailer.

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.540
One thing it doesn't take long to notice in
the "Stranger Things" Season 4 trailer is

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:23.310
how much older the main cast appears.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:29.529
In Season 1, Mike, Eleven, Will, Lucas, and
Dustin were all in the 11-13 range.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:33.280
And by Season 3 most of them were about 14
years old.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.870
Season 3 debuted almost three years ago at
this point, and the actors playing the kids

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:39.780
are all now young adults.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:44.460
By now the gang has graduated from attending
Hawkins Middle School to Hawkins High School,

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:47.730
or in Eleven and Will's case, Lenora Hills
High School.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:51.610
However, not all of them have adjusted well
to the change in schools.

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:56.079
Lucas seems to be doing fine as a member of
the Hawkins basketball team, but Eleven is

00:00:56.079 --> 00:00:58.620
still something of a social outcast.

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.640
While walking through the school halls, other
students barely acknowledge her, though her

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.850
friendship with Will is still strong.

00:01:04.850 --> 00:01:10.330
Still, the terrors of high school socialization
will probably be the least of her worries

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:16.613
as shady government organizations, and new
threats from the Upside Down, rear their ugly heads.

00:01:16.945 --> 00:01:19.369
"See you on the other side."

00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:21.110
"On the other side."

00:01:22.110 --> 00:01:27.740
Though looking a little worse for wear, David
Harbour's Jim Hopper is alive after somehow

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:32.060
being transported to Russia after seemingly
dying in the season three finale.

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:35.689
The only question is how Eleven and her friends
will get him back?

00:01:35.689 --> 00:01:40.070
Thankfully, the new trailer reveals that rescue
might come with the help of two old friends

00:01:40.070 --> 00:01:43.740
that we're pretty sure have no history of
flying airplanes.

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:49.960
In one frenetic clip, Joyce and Hawkins conspiracy
theorist, Murray Bauman, appear layered up

00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:54.200
for winter weather in a biplane going through
some major turbulence.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.289
Have they somehow tracked Hopper down and
set off on their own to rescue him from a

00:01:58.289 --> 00:01:59.289
Russian gulag?

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:06.899
"Stranger Things" wears its pop culture influences
on its sleeves, and Season 4 will once again

00:02:06.899 --> 00:02:08.590
honor the "X-Men."

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:13.110
In the latest trailer, Mike Wheeler and Eddie
Munson can be spotted wearing Hellfire Club

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:18.070
t-shirts, which is a reference to the fictional
society in the "X-Men" comic books whose members

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:21.560
have frequently crossed paths with the heroes
throughout the years.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:25.730
The Easter egg may have a deeper meaning than
just a nod to the X-Men.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:30.910
After all, "The Hellfire Club" is also the
name of the premiere episode of Season 4.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:37.060
Furthermore, a previous trailer hinted at
what could be another group of super-powered children.

00:02:37.060 --> 00:02:41.910
Whether that was a flashback to Eleven’s
time in the lab or an indication that there’s

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:46.260
another group of kids getting experimented
on, we’ll just have to wait and see.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:52.270
Either way, if season four follows up on this,
we may see the return of Eleven's "sister," Kali.

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:58.920
Of course, the "X-Men" influence on "Stranger
Things" has been evident since Season 1.

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:04.620
The very first chapter features a moment where
Will and Dustin discuss "Uncanny X-Men #134"

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:08.690
— the story that introduced Jean Grey's
Dark Phoenix persona.

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:13.260
Eleven’s arc in the show has drawn some
comparisons to Jean Grey in previous seasons;

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:17.910
considering that Dark Phoenix emerges after
a brush with the Hellfire Club in “X-Men,”

00:03:17.910 --> 00:03:23.480
fans may want to worry about how Eleven and
the Hellfire Club of “Stranger Things”

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:24.480
will intersect.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:31.750
Max Mayfield is featured front and center
in this brand new trailer for "Stranger Things."

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:36.200
Introduced in Season 2, Max has a bit of a
tomboy personality and is known for enjoying

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:38.280
video games, cars, and skateboards.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:41.820
Early in the trailer, we see her talking at
the grave of her brother Billy.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:47.400
Later, in front of the same grave, we see
Max levitating several feet above the ground

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:51.060
as her friends look on in absolute shock.

00:03:51.060 --> 00:03:56.370
The mechanism for her levitation is unknown
at this point, but there is definitely something

00:03:56.370 --> 00:03:58.280
supernatural going on.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:03.680
It could be some manifestation of her brother's
fatal possession in season three, or maybe

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.230
Max has inherited some kind of power from
the Upside Down.

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:12.970
Either way, it definitely looks like Max is
in for a wild ride, one that could put her

00:04:12.970 --> 00:04:16.769
on even footing with newfound telekinetic
bestie Eleven.

00:04:16.769 --> 00:04:19.250
"Him and Lucas are playing Atari right now."

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:20.500
"But friends don't lie."

00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:25.680
"But boyfriends lie, all the time."

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:30.180
Toward the end of the action-packed trailer,
there's a blink-and-you'll-miss-it shot of

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:33.880
horror icon Robert Englund with a pretty intense
look.

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:37.660
The star is best known for playing Freddy
Krueger in Wes Craven's "Nightmare on Elm

00:04:37.660 --> 00:04:42.230
St." franchise, a supernatural killer who
stalks the dreams of his victims to slaughter

00:04:42.230 --> 00:04:45.650
them in various inventive, grisly ways.

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:50.120
Freddie quickly earned his place in horror
history thanks to his unique design, and it's

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:56.240
clear that "Stranger Things" creators, the
Duffer Brothers, are huge fans of the movies.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:04:58.490
"There's nothing there.

00:04:58.490 --> 00:05:04.990
Dylan stop, you're scaring me."

00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:10.750
Englund's brief appearance in the trailer
reveals the first proper look at Victor Creel.

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:15.100
He's a patient at the Pennhurst Mental Hospital
who was committed for murders he perpetrated

00:05:15.100 --> 00:05:17.040
back in the 1960s.

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:23.310
He's clearly had a bad time since then because
aside from his bedraggled appearance, his

00:05:23.310 --> 00:05:27.510
eyes are heavily scarred, and it looks like
he's probably blind.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:32.900
It's not clear if Creel's injuries are self-inflicted,
or if they're the result of whatever seems

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.870
to be plaguing his ancestral home, the Creel
House.

00:05:35.870 --> 00:05:40.540
Either way, it's great to see Englund getting
to play with a creepy new character.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:46.780
Near the end of the trailer comes a dizzying
sequence of quick cuts, including a few brief

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:51.380
shots of a lone electric guitarist playing
atop a mobile home trailer, while red lightning

00:05:51.380 --> 00:05:53.130
flashes in the background.

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:58.840
The long-haired leather-clad musician appears
to be Eddie Munson, one of several new characters

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:00.900
to be introduced in Season 4.

00:06:00.900 --> 00:06:06.220
The dim lighting and cold colors suggest that
he may be in the Upside Down, and there are

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:11.530
heavy cables behind him that don't appear
to be necessary for guitar amplification.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:15.950
Whether he figures into the new season as
a hero or a villain, there’s no easy way

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:16.950
to tell from the trailer.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:23.500
Since "Stranger Things" debuted, the Hawkins
AV Club has fought the Demogorgon, the Flayed,

00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:25.280
and the hulking Mind-Flayer.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:30.770
But they're about to meet a terrifying new
Big Bad who looks like he's going to be more

00:06:30.770 --> 00:06:33.170
than a match for Eleven and the gang.

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:37.820
The trailer delivers its first jump scare
when a creepy monster opens its eyes.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:41.670
But it's not until the end of the footage
that we get a full look at it.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:48.020
The gray, fleshy creature is much more human
than the Demogorgon or the Mind-Flayer.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:53.140
It's highly likely that this unknown villain
is the one providing the narration at the

00:06:53.140 --> 00:07:00.000
beginning and end of the trailer, especially
since its full reveal comes with the intimidating line,

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:04.990
"You have lost."

00:07:04.990 --> 00:07:11.270
The creature's look is pretty gross, as it
has no nose, and its muscles are stretched

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:14.240
and warped across its entire body.

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:20.210
There are also a number of tentacles protruding
out of its back, and it can clearly use them

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:21.990
to move.

00:07:21.990 --> 00:07:27.800
Considering Season 4 is the beginning of the
end, it wouldn't be surprising if this new

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:31.310
evil will stick around for Season 5.

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:34.910
What this new monster has in store for the
kids of Hawkins is unknown.

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:41.210
We'll have to find out when "Stranger Things
4" Vol. 1 arrives on May 27.

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:46.030
"When you say date, just so we're crystal
clear about things..."

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:47.030
"Yeah, Hop?

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:49.430
Stop talking before I change my mind."

